B.L9=new A.bg("r02",B.bb,"A library notice","What can visitors do after 4 p.m. on Friday?",B.SP,1,"Oak Street Library will close at 4 p.m. on Friday for electrical repairs. Books can still be returned through the outside slot. The library will open as usual at 9 a.m. on Saturday.",B.A,null,B.T)
B.R9=s(["To buy food before the train","To change their tickets","To have breakfast with the driver"],t.s)
B.LD=new A.bg("r03",B.bb,"A message from Nora","Why does Nora want to meet at 9:50?",B.R9,0,"Hi Eli, our train now leaves at 10:20, not 10:50. Let\u2019s meet outside the station caf\xe9 at 9:50 so we have time to buy lunch. I already have both tickets. Nora",B.A,null,B.T)
B.RB=s(["Ben brought his broken desk lamp to the neighbourhood repair day.","At the welcome desk, a volunteer gave him a number and asked him to wait.","When his number was called, an electrician examined the lamp and replaced a loose wire.","Ben then tested the repaired lamp and thanked the electrician before taking it home."],t.s)
B.Lv=new A.bg("r04",B.bb,"A neighbourhood repair day",u.y,B.A,null,null,B.RB,null,B.c7)
B.QF=s(["In a school gym","At a different park","Inside the community hall"],t.s)
B.Lf=new A.bg("r05",B.bb,"An outdoor cinema","Where will the film be shown if heavy rain is expected?",B.QF,2,"The outdoor cinema in Meadow Park is free, but seats cannot be reserved. Gates open at 7 p.m., and the film begins after sunset. Bring a blanket because the grass may be damp. If heavy rain is forecast, the screening will move to the community hall.",B.A,null,B.T)
B.Q9=s(["A recommendation from his doctor","Delays on his usual route","A rise in bus fares"],t.s)
B.Lq=new A.bg("r06",B.bb,"Trying a different commute","What first persuaded Ravi to try cycling?",B.Q9,1,"For years, Ravi drove to work because he thought cycling would take too long. When roadworks doubled his journey time, he tried his bicycle. The ride took only twenty minutes, and he arrived feeling more alert. He now cycles most days, although he still takes the bus in icy weather.",B.A,null,B.T)
B.RN=s(["While unpacking after an art class, Jo noticed that her sketchbook was missing.","She phoned the studio and described the blue cover to the receptionist.","The receptionist found a matching book under a chair and kept it behind the desk.","The next morning, Jo returned to the studio to collect it."],t.s)
B.Lu=new A.bg("r07",B.bb,"A missing sketchbook",u.y,B.A,null,null,B.RN,null,B.c7)
B.Sw=s(["To connect objects with personal experiences","To remove all written information","To teach visitors how to record sound"],t.s)
B.L4=new A.bg("r08",B.bb,"A museum experiment","What is the main purpose of the recordings?",B.Sw,0,"The River Museum recently replaced some printed labels with recordings made by local residents. Visitors can hear personal memories connected to the objects. Although a few people prefer reading at their own pace, most say the voices make the collection feel closer to everyday life. Printed information remains available beside every object.",B.A,null,B.T)
B.QQ=s(["Customers rarely asked about books","The website was no longer used","There was substantial work beyond serving customers"],t.s)
B.Lg=new A.bg("r09",B.bb,"Working at a bookshop","What surprised Amira about her job?",B.QQ,2,"When Amira joined a small bookshop, she expected to spend most of her time recommending novels. Instead, she discovered that organising deliveries and updating the website were equally important. She still enjoys conversations with customers, but says the experience has taught her how much unseen work keeps a shop running.",B.A,null,B.T)
B.RO=s(["A group of students decided to make a podcast about the history of their school.","To gather stories for the first episode, they interviewed several former teachers.","After editing those interviews, they recorded an introduction and added music they had composed themselves.","They finally published the finished episode on the school website."],t.s)
B.LC=new A.bg("r10",B.bb,"A school podcast",u.y,B.A,null,null,B.RO,null,B.c7)
B.R7=s(["To reduce employees\u2019 salaries","To see whether the results would hold in other conditions","To replace quiet hours with more meetings"],t.s)
B.L3=new A.bg("r11",B.bb,"A flexible working trial","Why did the managers extend the trial?",B.R7,1,"A design firm tested a four-day working week without reducing pay. Staff agreed to shorten routine meetings and reserve quiet hours for concentrated work. Output remained stable during the three-month trial, but managers warned that a busy season might produce different results. They extended the experiment rather than making the change permanent immediately.",B.A,null,B.T)
B.R5=s(["Finding people who can inspect and maintain equipment","Persuading members to buy a full set of tools","Stopping members from sharing advice"],t.s)
B.LT=new A.bg("r12",B.bb,"Borrowing instead of buying","Which difficulty does the scheme need to manage?",B.R5,0,"A neighbourhood tool library lends equipment that many households use only occasionally. Its organisers say the main benefit is not simply saving money: members also exchange practical advice. However, every item must be checked on return, so the scheme relies on volunteers who know how to maintain the tools safely.",B.A,null,B.T)
B.So=s(["After winter storms damaged the riverside path, the council asked residents how it should be restored.","The responses favoured a permeable surface rather than replacing the old concrete.","Using that feedback, engineers designed a surface that would allow rainwater to drain through it.","Once the new design was approved, construction began on the first section of the path."],t.s)
B.Lh=new A.bg("r13",B.bb,"Restoring a riverside path",u.y,B.A,null,null,B.So,null,B.c7)
B.QU=s(["It should stop because attendance was lower","It succeeded only if it increased sales","Its value includes making shopping easier for some customers"],t.s)
B.LE=new A.bg("r14",B.bb,"A quiet shopping hour","What is the manager\u2019s view of the trial?",B.QU,2,"A supermarket introduced an hour with dimmer lights and no background music for customers who find busy shops overwhelming. The trial attracted fewer people than an ordinary hour, but those who attended stayed longer and reported feeling more comfortable. The manager argues that success should be measured by accessibility as well as sales.",B.A,null,B.T)
B.Qa=s(["The volunteers expected identical temperatures everywhere","They investigated a possible measurement problem","They abandoned their original research question"],t.s)
B.LN=new A.bg("r15",B.bb,"A community weather station","What does the response to the unusual readings show?",B.Qa,1,"Volunteers installed weather sensors across a town to compare temperatures in different streets. Early readings suggested that shaded areas were cooler, but one sensor consistently reported unusually low values. Rather than dismissing the whole project, the volunteers checked its position and discovered it was too close to a ventilation outlet. They moved it and continued collecting data.",B.A,null,B.T)
